WARNINGS AND NEAR-MISSES
  - The frontend-design skill flags "warm cream background plus high-contrast serif
    plus warm accent" as a known generated-design tell. The brief pins this direction,
    so it stands, but the build deliberately separates itself from that cluster: the
    accent is a dark rubric vermilion #8E1B12 rather than terracotta, and the page is
    carried by codex machinery (versals, scribe ruling, marginal glosses, ordinance
    table) rather than by cards and gradient washes.
  - Small caps are set with font-variant-caps on properly cased text, not
    text-transform uppercase, per the same skill's warning about all-caps labels.
  - The demo's selection-to-highlight action wraps a Range in a <mark>. Ranges that
    cross paragraph boundaries throw on extractContents, so the handler catches and
    reports it in voice instead of failing silently.
  - Gallery regeneration moved the two 2026-06-12 entries relative to each other
    because the rebuild sorts by (date, slug) for determinism. Content is unchanged.
    Every other slide is byte-identical to the previous build.

